with the data and there's
really a lot of possibilities

01:15:25.260 --> 01:15:26.130
you can do with this.

01:15:26.130 --> 01:15:28.890
You can make all kinds of shiny apps.

01:15:28.890 --> 01:15:29.723
You don't even have to make a shiny app.

01:15:29.723 --> 01:15:32.960
You can just play with a
single leaflet interactive map

01:15:32.960 --> 01:15:35.180
hope this was helpful

01:15:35.180 --> 01:15:38.290
and hope that you guys end up making

01:15:38.290 --> 01:15:41.510
some even better visualizations than this,

01:15:41.510 --> 01:15:43.210
showing all kinds of creative stuff.

01:15:43.210 --> 01:15:46.790
You can take this stuff to, to
not just apply to COVID data,

01:15:46.790 --> 01:15:47.980
of course you can take this

01:15:47.980 --> 01:15:50.430
and apply it to whatever
your favorite data set is,

01:15:50.430 --> 01:15:55.430
we are talking about COVID-19
the most important thing

01:15:56.710 --> 01:16:00.140
is transparency and
understanding of the data.

01:16:00.140 --> 01:16:02.670
And again, I will just say,
as I said in the other video

01:16:02.670 --> 01:16:07.073
that when putting out
data viz for COVID-19

01:16:08.470 --> 01:16:12.510
just always ask yourself first
like what new information

01:16:12.510 --> 01:16:15.470
is the data viz showing that
hasn't already been shown?

01:16:15.470 --> 01:16:17.240
Does this serve a public need?

01:16:17.240 --> 01:16:21.850
Is this, will this be
wildly misinterpreted?

01:16:21.850 --> 01:16:24.360
Have I done everything
possible to make sure

01:16:24.360 --> 01:16:25.940
that enough context has been provided

01:16:25.940 --> 01:16:27.130
for this visualization?

01:16:27.130 --> 01:16:28.580
And the data is solid?

01:16:28.580 --> 01:16:30.920
The responsibility is
unfortunately too high

01:16:30.920 --> 01:16:32.815
for something like COVID viz

01:16:32.815 --> 01:16:35.600
to be kind of careless with that, right?

01:16:35.600 --> 01:16:37.590
So always keep that in mind.

01:16:37.590 --> 01:16:39.670
But again, the data is
out there to play with

01:16:39.670 --> 01:16:42.010
and practice on your own time always.

01:16:42.010 --> 01:16:44.650
So whether or not you decide to publish

01:16:45.570 --> 01:16:48.230
some of this data, I think, you know

01:16:48.230 --> 01:16:50.700
there's a lot you can do with the data

01:16:50.700 --> 01:16:52.840
even just to understand for yourself

01:16:52.840 --> 01:16:55.440
like how these visualizations are made

01:16:55.440 --> 01:16:57.120
and think about maybe the best ways

01:16:57.120 --> 01:16:59.220
you would wanna visualize it for yourself.

